# git
PKG_VER=2.55.0
PKG_URL="https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/git-${PKG_VER}.tar.xz"
PKG_DEPS="lfs/zlib lfs/openssl lfs/curl lfs/expat lfs/pcre2 lfs/perl5"
BUILD_PROCESS=configmake
### The make of git builds only in the source tree: the configure generates config.mak.autogen
### next to the sources the main Makefile includes
PKG_COPYSRC=1
### --with-libpcre2 brings -P to git grep, --without-tcltk leaves gitk out: there is no tcl in lfs
CONF_FLAGS="--with-libpcre2 --without-tcltk"
### The configure of git probes the platform with three test programs it cannot run while cross
### compiling: the cache variables answer for them, what glibc does
### - iconv does not omit the BOM for utf-16 and utf-32
### - fopen of a directory succeeds (the fread after it fails)
### - snprintf conforms to C99
CONF_VARS="ac_cv_iconv_omits_bom=no ac_cv_fread_reads_directories=yes ac_cv_snprintf_returns_bogus=no"
### The perl scripts (Git.pm and the commands of libexec/git-core) look for their modules in the
### site_perl of lfs/perl5: PERL_VER of setenv is the same version the perl5 recipe builds. The
### recipe checksum of git does not change when PERL_VER does, so bumping perl means rebuilding
### git too (build --force, or just delete the status file)
### NO_RUST leaves the Rust subsystems out: cargo builds their build scripts for the host with
### the RUSTFLAGS of the target and the LLVM of the host toolchain refuses them
### In cross the configure finds the headers of curl but no curl-config in the PATH and records
### an empty CURL_LDFLAGS, which overrides the -lcurl default of the Makefile: set it here
PKG_MAKEVARS="NO_RUST=1 CURL_LDFLAGS=-lcurl perllibdir=${INSTALL_LIBDIR}${INSTALL_LIBSUFFIX}/perl5/$(echo ${PERL_VER} | cut -d. -f1,2)/site_perl"
### The release tarball ships no prebuilt manual: git help falls back to the web pages
